            {
                "entry_id": "28d13dc4-0575-3605-9b84-643f062a7d4a",
                "word": "neo",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d095375a-7fc7-4a9a-b64c-df5994d77a2c",
                        "entry_id": "28d13dc4-0575-3605-9b84-643f062a7d4a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "neos"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bfb89e5e-ee09-31b6-9a57-2d91fb4fada1",
                        "entry_id": "28d13dc4-0575-3605-9b84-643f062a7d4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Clipping of neofan."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "clipping",
                            "dated",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac751471-d6a3-4431-921d-d53812f2fff5",
                                "sense_id": "bfb89e5e-ee09-31b6-9a57-2d91fb4fada1",
                                "text": "Ken Bulmer pointed out that the attitude of a fan who had read much sf is different from that of a neo who is reading sf for the first time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ea1bc3d-955e-4a17-a00c-6c387525bd95",
                                "sense_id": "bfb89e5e-ee09-31b6-9a57-2d91fb4fada1",
                                "text": "This fabulous fannish cover illustrated the three stages of fandom: the neo, the trufan, and the BNF."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdb834d7-bfc7-4c3a-b638-b9aeb1ef5e28",
                                "sense_id": "bfb89e5e-ee09-31b6-9a57-2d91fb4fada1",
                                "text": "Edwina, and neofen of her generation (this is not a criticism - everyone starts out as a neo), being new to sffandom, and not a member of faandom, would not have noticed this."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43db8249-2d19-3374-9f98-553292a04724",
                        "entry_id": "28d13dc4-0575-3605-9b84-643f062a7d4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Clipping of neoconservative."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "clipping"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d42da42-bde1-4934-80c9-67ad9b331a92",
                                "sense_id": "43db8249-2d19-3374-9f98-553292a04724",
                                "text": "The neos seem to be no less uncomfortable with the paleos than the paleos are with the neos, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3de3e1ae-48ec-44e7-be9c-41d1f9c3f159",
                                "sense_id": "43db8249-2d19-3374-9f98-553292a04724",
                                "text": "Some say the neos are good for what ails us on both foreign and domestic fronts, while others are quick to debate that."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a526c117-3cef-3909-9318-251643c4175d",
                        "entry_id": "28d13dc4-0575-3605-9b84-643f062a7d4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Clipping of neopronoun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "clipping",
                            "in-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "352204a9-1040-39d8-9ece-832434e9409a",
                        "entry_id": "28d13dc4-0575-3605-9b84-643f062a7d4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Clipping of neodymium."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "clipping"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2457afd-9b19-4b71-878c-8dabf0df31d5",
                                "sense_id": "352204a9-1040-39d8-9ece-832434e9409a",
                                "text": "The most important application of dysprosium and terbium, which belong to a subgroup known as the heavy rare earths, is in devices called neodymium boron magnets, or neo magnets for short."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
